@ Co-op scene test. Run it from BOTH consoles (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 1).
@
@ Whoever runs it first should stop on the message below until the other one
@ runs it too, then both should see the rest together. Run it with the other
@ player on a different map and it should refuse instead.
Debug_EventScript_Script_1::
	coopscene GATE_TEST
	lockall
	msgbox CoopText_TestBothHere, MSGBOX_DEFAULT
	coopgate GATE_TEST_SECOND
	msgbox CoopText_TestStillTogether, MSGBOX_DEFAULT
	releaseall
	end

@ Co-op gift test. Run it from ONE console (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 2).
@
@ Both players should end up with three Potions between them -- not three each.
@ The bag is shared, so the player who did not trigger it must not add a second
@ lot of its own; goto_if_coop_guest is what stops it.
Debug_EventScript_Script_2::
	coopscene GATE_TEST_GIFT
	lockall
	goto_if_coop_guest Debug_EventScript_Script_2_Done
	additem ITEM_POTION, 3
Debug_EventScript_Script_2_Done:
	releaseall
	end

@ Co-op presence test (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 3). This is the shape the gym
@ leaders use: not mirrored, just refused when you are on your own. One Potion
@ into the shared bag if it went ahead, nothing at all if it did not.
Debug_EventScript_Script_3::
	coop_require_partner
	lockall
	additem ITEM_POTION, 1
	releaseall
	end

@ Co-op battle test (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 4). Run it from ONE console;
@ the scene mirrors it to the other and both of you end up in the same battle
@ against the two Rustboro gym trainers.
Debug_EventScript_Script_4::
	coopscene GATE_TEST_BATTLE
	lockall
	coopbattle TRAINER_JOSH, TRAINER_TOMMY
	releaseall
	end

@ Co-op battle test, part one (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 5). Run it on EACH
@ console separately -- it is not a co-op scene -- then run Script 4 to fight.
@ Something strong enough to win a test battle without careful play.
Debug_EventScript_Script_5::
	@ From empty, so the party is the same six however the console got here.
	@ givemon only fills free slots, and a fresh co-op game now starts every
	@ player with a starter -- which sat at the front of this team and took
	@ the battle into a fight nobody meant to test.
	callnative Debug_ClearParty
	givemon SPECIES_SWAMPERT, 50
	givemon SPECIES_SCEPTILE, 50
	givemon SPECIES_BLAZIKEN, 50
	givemon SPECIES_GARDEVOIR, 50
	givemon SPECIES_AGGRON, 50
	givemon SPECIES_FLYGON, 50
	release
	end

@ Co-op SPLIT battle test (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 6). Run on ONE console.
@ Roxanne's whole team dealt across herself and a filler partner: the same
@ Pokemon she always had, fought as a double battle. Her gym keeps all of its
@ own trainers.
Debug_EventScript_Script_6::
	coopscene GATE_TEST_BATTLE
	lockall
	coopbattle_split TRAINER_ROXANNE_1, TRAINER_JOSH
	releaseall
	end

@ Co-op GYM PATTERN test (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 7). Run on ONE console.
@ Exactly the shape the real gyms use: mirror the script, mark the next
@ battle, then an ordinary trainerbattle that keeps all its own machinery.
Debug_EventScript_Script_7::
	coopscene GATE_TEST_BATTLE
	coopnextbattle_split TRAINER_JOSH
	@ no_intro rather than single: the full form wants a trainer object event
	@ on the map to walk up to the player, and the debug menu has none.
	trainerbattle_no_intro TRAINER_ROXANNE_1, RustboroCity_Gym_Text_RoxanneDefeat
	goto Debug_EventScript_CoopGymWon
	end

Debug_EventScript_CoopGymWon::
	msgbox CoopText_TestStillTogether, MSGBOX_DEFAULT
	release
	end

@ Co-op BOX test (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 8). Run Script 5 first to fill the
@ party, then this on ONE console: the party is full, so the Pokemon goes to
@ the PC -- and should appear in the other player's PC too.
Debug_EventScript_Script_8::
	givemon SPECIES_LATIAS, 50
	release
	end

@ Co-op REAL GYM test (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 9). Run it on EACH console --
@ it is not a co-op scene, each player warps itself.
@
@ Everything up to now has been tested against debug scripts that imitate the
@ gym pattern. This drops both players into Rustboro Gym itself, one tile below
@ Roxanne, so the next Up+A runs the real RustboroCity_Gym_EventScript_Roxanne
@ off the real object event: the gate, the mirrored scene, the filler partner
@ and trainerbattle_single's own bookkeeping, none of which a debug script
@ exercises.
@
@ (5,3) is the tile south of her at (5,2). Walking Up into her is blocked, so
@ the input turns the player to face her instead of moving.
Debug_EventScript_Script_9::
	setvar VAR_RUSTBORO_CITY_STATE, 1
	warp MAP_RUSTBORO_CITY_GYM, 5, 3
	waitstate
	release
	end

@ Co-op REAL GYM test, the 6v6 (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 10). Run on EACH
@ console. Lands below Josh at (5,13) -- the one fight in the gym that is two
@ real trainers with full teams rather than one team dealt across two slots.
Debug_EventScript_Script_10::
	setvar VAR_RUSTBORO_CITY_STATE, 1
	warp MAP_RUSTBORO_CITY_GYM, 5, 14
	waitstate
	release
	end

@ Co-op PERSISTENCE test (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 11). Run on PLAYER 2.
@ Gives one Pokemon and spends some money. Both have to reach the other
@ console: the party through the record resend, the money through a delta.
@
@ Spends rather than earns. The debug save starts at MAX_MONEY, so addmoney
@ is a no-op there and a test built on it passes whether or not anything is
@ shared -- which is exactly what the first version of this did.
@ removemoney goes FIRST. givemon runs a waitstate for the "got a Pokemon"
@ flow, and nothing after it in a debug-menu script runs -- which looked
@ exactly like money not being shared.
Debug_EventScript_Script_11::
	removemoney 4242, 0
	givemon SPECIES_LATIOS, 50
	release
	end

@ Co-op FOLLOW test (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 12). Run on ONE console.
@ The same pair of things Fly does: announce the trip, then take it. The
@ partner should arrive in the gym under their own steam.
Debug_EventScript_Script_12::
	coopfollowme
	warp MAP_RUSTBORO_CITY_GYM, 8, 15
	waitstate
	release
	end

@ Co-op ORDINARY WARP test (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 13). Run on ONE console.
@ No coopfollowme: the partner must NOT be dragged along. Every door in the
@ game is a warp like this one.
Debug_EventScript_Script_13::
	warp MAP_RUSTBORO_CITY, 16, 40
	waitstate
	release
	end

@ MID-GAME TEST SAVE (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 14). Run on PLAYER 1 only,
@ then Script 15 to save.
@
@ The point is to start a playtest somewhere worth testing rather than in a
@ bedroom: every HM usable, a team that can carry them, and supplies.
@
@ It ends by jumping into Debug_CheatStart, which is the maintained way to
@ put a save past the intro -- badges, Pokedex, running shoes, every town
@ marked visited so Fly works, and the story flags.
@
@ Those flags are the whole reason this is a goto rather than a handful of
@ setflags. The first version of this stamped badges onto a brand-new game
@ and nothing else, which produced a save with eight badges and a story that
@ had never started: walk into the grass on Route 101 and Birch still runs up
@ to hand you a starter, on both consoles, at different speeds.
@
@ The extras go FIRST because Debug_CheatStart ends the script.
Debug_EventScript_Script_14::
	giveitem ITEM_HM_CUT
	giveitem ITEM_HM_FLY
	giveitem ITEM_HM_SURF
	giveitem ITEM_HM_STRENGTH
	giveitem ITEM_HM_FLASH
	giveitem ITEM_HM_ROCK_SMASH
	giveitem ITEM_HM_WATERFALL
	giveitem ITEM_HM_DIVE
	giveitem ITEM_HYPER_POTION, 20
	giveitem ITEM_FULL_RESTORE, 10
	giveitem ITEM_REVIVE, 10
	giveitem ITEM_ULTRA_BALL, 30
	giveitem ITEM_ESCAPE_ROPE, 5
	givemon SPECIES_SWAMPERT, 50
	givemon SPECIES_SWELLOW, 50
	givemon SPECIES_GARDEVOIR, 50
	givemon SPECIES_AGGRON, 50
	givemon SPECIES_FLYGON, 50
	givemon SPECIES_MANECTRIC, 50
	goto Debug_CheatStart
	end

@ Clears the Player 2 slot and saves (R+Start, Scripts…, Script 15). Run it
@ after Script 14, on Player 1.
@
@ Clearing matters. A save generated with a partner console attached comes out
@ with that partner's character already in the Player 2 slot, and the next
@ person to join is handed it -- their name and the boy/girl they just chose
@ are overwritten by somebody else's. The first save shipped from here did
@ exactly that.
Debug_EventScript_Script_15::
	callnative Debug_ClearCoopPlayer2
	callnative Debug_SaveNow
	release
	end

@ PAST THE OPENING (R+Start, Scripts..., Script 19). Run on ONE console --
@ these are shared, so they reach the partner by themselves.
@
@ The story state Debug_CheatStart leaves behind, without the Pokemon, the
@ Pokedex or the bike. The co-op checks are about the co-op machinery, and a
@ fresh game drops both players into a town whose own story is still trying
@ to happen around them: Oak stopping you at the edge of Pallet Town, Birch's
@ twin sending you to Route 101, mum and the running shoes. Every one of
@ those is a mirrored scene now, which is right in play and means a test
@ measuring something else is forever being interrupted by one.
Debug_EventScript_Script_19::
	setflag FLAG_SYS_POKEMON_GET
	setflag FLAG_RESCUED_BIRCH
	setflag FLAG_HIDE_ROUTE_101_BIRCH_ZIGZAGOON_BATTLE
	setflag FLAG_ADVENTURE_STARTED
	setflag FLAG_HIDE_ROUTE_101_BIRCH_STARTERS_BAG
	setflag FLAG_RECEIVED_RUNNING_SHOES
	setflag FLAG_SYS_B_DASH
	setvar VAR_BIRCH_LAB_STATE, 5
	setvar VAR_ROUTE101_STATE, 3
	setvar VAR_LITTLEROOT_TOWN_STATE, 4
	setvar VAR_LITTLEROOT_INTRO_STATE, 7
	setvar VAR_LITTLEROOT_HOUSES_STATE_BRENDAN, 2
	setvar VAR_LITTLEROOT_HOUSES_STATE_MAY, 2
	setvar VAR_LITTLEROOT_RIVAL_STATE, 4
	setvar VAR_MAP_SCENE_PALLET_TOWN_OAK, 1
	release
	end

@ TO ROUTE 101, AT THE START OF THE STORY (R+Start, Scripts..., Script 18).
@
@ For the opening check. It puts the console on Route 101 in the state the
@ game is in when you first walk out of Littleroot, so the Birch chase and
@ his bag are both still ahead -- which is the part of the game that has to
@ work as co-op and the part that is an hour of walking to reach honestly.
@
@ Run on ONE console: it is a plain warp, and the partner follows by the
@ ordinary travel-together route.
Debug_EventScript_Script_18::
	setvar VAR_ROUTE101_STATE, 0
	setvar VAR_LITTLEROOT_TOWN_STATE, 2
	warp MAP_ROUTE101, 8, 15
	waitstate
	release
	end

@ A CONVERSATION, ON DEMAND (R+Start, Scripts..., Script 16).
@
@ Several checks need one console to be mid-conversation while something
@ happens on the other -- "your partner is busy" is a state the mirrored
@ scenes and the gates both have to handle, and it is not a state a test can
@ assert its way into.
@
@ It used to be staged by walking up to the television in the player's bedroom
@ and pressing A, which worked for exactly as long as the opening left both
@ players standing in that bedroom. Skipping the opening put them outside, in
@ a town with nothing within reach to talk to, and the check could no longer
@ set up the situation it was testing.
@
@ This is that conversation, reachable from anywhere: it locks the player and
@ waits for a button, which is what talking to anything amounts to.
Debug_EventScript_Script_16::
	lock
	faceplayer
	msgbox Debug_Text_CoopBusy, MSGBOX_DEFAULT
	release
	end

@ LOCKSTEP DIALOGUE TEST (R+Start, Scripts..., Script 17). Run on ONE console.
@
@ Four message boxes in a mirrored scene, with no gate between them. Script 1
@ has gates either side of its boxes, so the two consoles were pulled back
@ level whatever happened in between and the thing that drifts was never under
@ test. This is the shape a real story scene has: a run of boxes paced only by
@ whoever is pressing A.
Debug_EventScript_Script_17::
	coopscene GATE_TEST_LOCKSTEP
	lockall
	msgbox Debug_Text_CoopLockstep1, MSGBOX_DEFAULT
	msgbox Debug_Text_CoopLockstep2, MSGBOX_DEFAULT
	msgbox Debug_Text_CoopLockstep3, MSGBOX_DEFAULT
	msgbox Debug_Text_CoopLockstep4, MSGBOX_DEFAULT
	releaseall
	end

